<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    What a friendship group is named for (Source/ColonyCouncil/Social/Groups/GroupDefs.cs, GroupShareDef; GroupNaming.cs
    ranks them). A group bound by friendship alone is never named after one of its people: it takes its name from what
    most of them share, the more of them the sooner (Hours: more than half keep the night hours; Work: more than half do
    that work; Likeness: two in three have that side), else from a habit of theirs and its place in the group's own order,
    else from their friendship. Among a share's names that fit the colony's era and no group now (or lately) has, one is
    picked for the group and kept. A group of any other kind whose own names are all taken is named the same way.

    names: era tags as in flavour lines ([lowtech], [!lowtech], [tribal], [medieval], [industrial], [spacer]); never a
    person's name, nor "'s" (that is how names after someone read, and older saves are found by it).
    why: what the card says the group is, for a friendship group named for this share.
  -->

  <!-- ===================== Their habit and its place ===================== -->

